    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics was always a challenge for me, especially during my studies. I struggled more with abstract concepts like algebra and calculus compared to practical subjects like economics or biology. My parents didn't have formal education, so I had to rely on my own efforts to understand it. Over time, I learned that persistence is key—even if it doesn’t come naturally.",
